diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..d8d5411 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -159,3 +159,18 @@ __Response:__
 ```
 
 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+## Receiving events
+
+When a subscribed event happens on the board, Fizzy sends one `POST` to the webhook's payload URL. Each event is delivered exactly once per webhook.
+
+The request includes:
+
+- `Content-Type: application/json`
+- `User-Agent: fizzy/1.0.0 Webhook`
+- `X-Webhook-Timestamp`: when the request was sent, as UTC ISO-8601
+- `X-Webhook-Signature`: hex-encoded HMAC-SHA256 of the raw request body, using the webhook's signing secret
+
+Generic endpoints receive the event as JSON (`id`, `action`, `created_at`, `eventable`, `board`, `creator`). Slack, Campfire, and Basecamp chat URLs receive a short message instead: `{ "text" }`, `{ "body" }`, and `{ "content" }` respectively.
+
+The delivery log records the request headers (without the signature) and how the request went. A `2xx` response is a success. Anything else, including a connection failure, is a failure. Ten consecutive failures inside an hour switch the webhook off; reactivate it to try again. Delivery logs are kept for one week.
